Design and Manufacturing II — MIT 2.008, 2025 (@mech-mit-manufacturing: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mech-sources) { r_2FHEWYSEAHBY7X6030TW00F32E
Jung-Hoon Chun and Josh Ramos, MIT 2.008, Spring 2025. [Course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-008-design-and-manufacturing-ii-spring-2025/), [lecture notes](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-008-design-and-manufacturing-ii-spring-2025/lists/lecture-notes/), [homework](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-008-design-and-manufacturing-ii-spring-2025/lists/homework/) and [project](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-008-design-and-manufacturing-ii-spring-2025/pages/yo-yo-project/).

Complete the available sequence and substantial exercises after the mechanical foundations. Topics include polymer processes, machining, assembly/joining, variation and quality, casting/forming, additive production, planning, costs and manufacturing systems. The course's batch project illustrates integration; its particular product and batch size are not requirements of this learning route.

The course index and selected injection-molding, cutting, assembly, variation/control, cost, forming and additive PDFs were inspected on 30 October 2026. Some files are brief activities rather than full textbook chapters. OCW's CC BY-NC-SA terms apply subject to stated third-party exceptions; PDFs explicitly identify some excluded material. Course media, problem sets and software remain external references.

**Return:** [Mechanical-engineering sources](../Sources.lingua#r_06RZYPZEFNMZ6MZ690QB1WN1Z2).
